hat queenie is an  incredibly gifted legitimate born with  the innate ability to enter another  witch or wizard's mind and interpret  their thoughts she doesn't seem all that  confident in her abilities or position  as a witch she seems insistent that tina  or tini as she affectionately refers to  her sister is the career woman out of  the two of them and that all she does is  get coffee or fix the toilets  to me this suggests that quinny doesn't  put too much emphasis on pursuing higher  achievements within a more traditional  wizarding career path say that of  becoming an aura or professor that kind  of thing  perhaps she simply wasn't interested or  maybe she thought putting her magical  abilities into a career was a waste of  time whatever the reason it's pretty  clear that queenie doesn't put all that  much thought into her magic another  example of this is the way that she  reads people apologizing to newt's  commander after looking into his mind  without his permission  i know i'm sorry i can't help it people  are easiest to read when they're hurting  she says  in this instance it's clear that she  doesn't even have to try when practicing  legitimacy rather it just comes to her  so in my opinion it's her lack of  interest in magical pursuits that make  her so open to her attraction to jacob  kowalski the american nomads she meets  alongside newt in fact not only does she  seem accepting of his presence she seems  utterly fascinated a real life no manage  in her brownstone  so when the movie ends with her visiting  jacob in his bakery it's really not all  that surprising of course the next film  picks up with the two of them wrapped up  in a magically induced engagement  courtesy of queenie to me it all seems a  bit odd but i guess the logic behind it  makes sense as the audience will have to  deduce that between the two movies jacob  and queenie became romantically involved  however not in any formal way due to the  macusa laws which at the time forbade  witc